==Restrictions==
Rarity: Only [[:Category:Special Cats|Special]] and [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]]

==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 10~166.67 seconds<sup>300f~5,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Li'l Mohawk Cat (Enemy)|Li'l Mohawk Cat]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Teacher Bear]]s spawn, delay 73.33~80 seconds<sup>2,200f~2,400f</sup>.
**3 [[Professor A.|Professor As]] spawn, delay 126.67 seconds<sup>3,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Essentially the introduction to {{4c}} difficulty restrictions, all the units you can use are very limited and quite few.
This stage is similar to [[Deathhawk (Deadly)|Deathhawk]]; while Li'l Mohawk Cat has lower stats than [[Manic Mohawk Cat (Enemy)|Manic Mohawk Cat]], the real difficulty comes from the Professor As, since few {{4c}} options exist this early into the game.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Red Riding Mina]]: Essential for pretty much every lineup, her accessibility compared to other units listed (especially Prisoner) makes her a staple in sniping Prof. A and the enemy base. If one has beaten [[Legend Stages|Stories of Legend]], it is very recommended to grab her True Form, as it will double her DPS and slightly increase her effective range. Pairing her up with cheap 75¢ meatshields is the best way to defend her.
*[[Cat God the Great (Special Cat)|Cat God the Great]]: He makes this stage quite trivial, as his [[Omni Strike]] reaches up to 850 range. Since Omni Strike units stop at max range relative to the enemy base, this allows him to hit every enemy on the battlefield with his [[Knockback]] and huge damage, or even potentially cheese the stage without having to kill Li'l Mohawk. He fares much worse when not near the enemy base because of his low health and poor standing range, so keep him well protected with strong meatshields like [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]].
*[[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]]: Very resilient against everything that isn't Prof A, its high health and cheap price makes it a very effective option. Its slow speed means it needs time to catch up, but it also helps make even smaller gaps between meatshields to prevent Li'l Mohawk from pushing even further.
*[[Adult Cat (Rare Cat)|Prisoner Cat]]: With his naturally long range combined with piercing range, he is perfect for sniping the Professor As out from behind Li'l Mohawk, helping to remove a lot of difficulty from this stage.
*[[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando Jr.]]: Being tailor-made to destroy Traitless enemies, he naturally excels in this stage. He is able to easily keep Li'l Mohawk at bay with his rapid Knockbacks, while his Surges will help destroy Teacher Bear and Professor A. in the back, though bringing another unit to help with Professor A. is still recommended.
*[[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]]: With a 100% chance to weaken any enemy it hits to 50%, Thaumaturge can prove useful for stalling Li'l Mohawk by reducing its pushing power to half. However, she is very fragile and will die to Professor A very quickly, so make sure to protect her well.
*[[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]]: Acts like a temporary base if you don't want the enemies chipping away at your base while you stack LD units, has extremely high health that can last for a long time.

